  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"/>Keep both <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8217;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> together, then apart from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8217;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> other alphabets can be arranged in <math><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> ways. In the gaps, two <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8217;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> can be placed in <math><msub><mrow><mmultiscripts><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> ways.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><menclose notation=\"box\"><mi>OO</mi></menclose></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the total number of ways<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#8901;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none/><mprescripts/><mrow/><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p>",
